THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL IS NOT DISTRIBUTED IN THIS REPOSITORY
----------------------------------------------------------
The design and mathematics this project implements belong to Christopher
Carlson.  His original Wolfram Language source, his example notebook, and the
published figures and article copies that were used while checking this work
against his are copyrighted by their author, are not ours to redistribute, and
are therefore NOT included in a clone of this repository.  They exist only in
the author's own working copy (mstp/, refs/), and .gitignore lists them so they
cannot be committed by accident.

The fidelity checks that those figures were used for are described in
HANDOFF.md, and the automated gates compare the app against dev/port.py, a
Python model written from Carlson's published description of the geometry.

The engine in src/engine.js is an independent reimplementation, written in
JavaScript, of the geometry and algorithm Carlson publishes.  It is not a
translation of his source file, and no code from his file is copied into it.

